## Context

The Click & Read resolver sends some DOIs to PANIST, an INIST archive of
current subscriptions, not to the BibCNRS proxy. Its API is shaped like
ISTEX's. Observed on 2026-11-11:

- Metadata search is open: `https://api.panist.fr/document/?q=doi:"<doi>"`
  returns the document id, and `/document/<id>/` its record.
- Full text is at `/document/<id>/fulltext/pdf`; without a session it answers
  302 to `/authFede/` (federated login).
- `/corpus` lists four collections: elsevier 11,301,473 documents, springer
  1,107,896, iop 252,253, aps 149,894.

On a list of 80 paywalled DOIs (climate-finance-het, its ticket 2882), 9 were
held by PANIST: 7 Elsevier and 2 Springer. A logged-in browser downloaded
them; the tool has no route to them, and the proxy route to the same articles
goes through publisher sites that resist scripted clients.

Not established: whether the API accepts a token, as ISTEX does, or only a
browser session.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A `panist` source: open DOI lookup, then the full text with the configured credential (token or cookie file, whichever the API supports); skipped with a clear message when unconfigured
- [ ] Placed in the default cascade beside ISTEX; `--help` and the README document its configuration
- [ ] Offline tests with fixtures for found, not found and unauthenticated
